# The HUD and the quick views in the user's units, set on CONFIG's Planner page.
#
# CurrentState's getters multiply alt, airspeed, groundspeed, wp_dist, DistToHome and the rest by
# multiplieralt, multiplierspeed or multiplierdist (ExtLibs/ArduPilot/CurrentState.cs:327, 354,
# 496, 529, 1093, 1781), which MainV2.ChangeUnits sets from the Planner page's unit combos
# (MainV2.cs:4254-4337, ConfigPlanner.cs:558-571, 1050-1055); FlightData.Activate names the units
# on the HUD (GCSViews/FlightData.cs:444-446), and each quick view's description names its unit
# through GetNameandUnit (CurrentState.cs:4529-4555). The HUD draws its speed and AS/GS lines with
# speedunit, its altitude with altunit and the waypoint distance with distunit
# (ExtLibs/Controls/HUD.cs:2552-2577, 2735, 2751-2771).
#
# The claim: with nothing set everything is in metres and metres per second; after Feet, Feet and
# knots on the Planner page, the HUD's facts and the quick views' descriptions name ft and kts,
# and a quick view bound to the altitude above sea level reads it in feet - SITL's default home,
# CMAC, is 584 m up, so the number goes from 58x to 191x. The multipliers and every text are
# proved exactly by the unit tests in crates/mp-gui/src/hud.rs and quick.rs; this proves the
# Planner page's units reach the HUD and the quick views in the running application.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760, on the ground at its default home and past its
# start-up (GPS locked, so the altitude above sea level is in). The Planner page's keys are in the
# per-run settings file, so every run starts in metres; the quick views' choices go into a scratch
# config.xml. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/hud-units.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 12

# Metres and metres per second, as ChangeUnits sets them with nothing configured.
expect hud.speed ~ m/s
expect hud.airspeed ~ m/s
expect hud.groundspeed ~ m/s
expect hud.wpdist ~ m>
expect fly.quick.1.label Altitude (m)
expect fly.quick.2.label GroundSpeed (m/s)
expect fly.quick.3.label Dist to WP (m)
expect fly.quick.4.label Yaw (deg)
expect fly.quick.5.label Vertical Speed (m/s)
expect fly.quick.6.label Dist to Home (m)

# The first view on the altitude above sea level: CMAC's 584 m.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
doubleclick fly-quick-1
expect fly.quick.chooser 1
click fly-quick-choice-altasl
expect fly.quick.1 altasl
expect fly.quick.1.label Altitude (m)
expect fly.quick.1.value ~ 58

# CONFIG's Planner page: Feet for distance and altitude, knots for speed.
click tab-config
click config-page-ConfigPlanner
expect config.page ConfigPlanner
click planner-CMB_distunits
click planner-CMB_distunits-Feet
click planner-CMB_altunits
click planner-CMB_altunits-Feet
click planner-CMB_speedunits
click planner-CMB_speedunits-knots
expect config.planner.units.dist ft
expect config.planner.units.alt ft
expect config.planner.units.speed kts

# Back on the flight screen, the HUD names the units and the views read in them.
click tab-fly
expect hud.speed ~ kts
expect hud.airspeed ~ kts
expect hud.groundspeed ~ kts
expect hud.alt ~ ft
expect hud.wpdist ~ ft>
expect fly.quick.1 altasl
expect fly.quick.1.label Altitude (ft)
# 584 m is 1916 ft.
expect fly.quick.1.value ~ 191
expect fly.quick.2.label GroundSpeed (kts)
expect fly.quick.3.label Dist to WP (ft)
expect fly.quick.4.label Yaw (deg)
expect fly.quick.5.label Vertical Speed (kts)
expect fly.quick.6.label Dist to Home (ft)

# And back to metres: the same view reads metres again.
click tab-config
click planner-CMB_altunits
click planner-CMB_altunits-Meters
expect config.planner.units.alt m
click tab-fly
expect hud.alt ~ m
expect fly.quick.1.label Altitude (m)
expect fly.quick.1.value ~ 58
# Speed and distance stay as they were set.
expect hud.speed ~ kts
expect fly.quick.3.label Dist to WP (ft)
